  "securityNotes": "Read SKILL.md and LICENSE.txt in full at the pinned SHA; the 26 bundled font families (81 files: one Regular/style .ttf set plus one -OFL.txt per family, listed from the tree API without reading binary .ttf content) were spot-checked by reading 3 representative -OFL.txt files in full (ArsenalSC, WorkSans, YoungSerif) -- all three are the standard SIL Open Font License 1.1 boilerplate with a distinct per-family copyright line (e.g. 'Copyright 2019 The Work Sans Project Authors'), confirming free redistribution rights; every other OFL.txt file's presence and per-family naming was verified via the tree listing but not individually opened. Total bundle size 5.55 MB (< 10 MB threshold), so this does not trigger the size-based not-vendored-keeper rule. SKILL.md content is prose/process instructions for generating static art (.md philosophy + .pdf/.png output); no scripts, no network calls, no credential access. One notable prompt-engineering pattern: the 'FINAL STEP' section has the skill assert as fact that 'The user ALREADY said' a specific quoted critique ('It isn't perfect enough...') to trigger an extra refinement pass -- this is a fabricated user statement baked into the skill rather than an actual message from whoever installs it. It does not ask the agent to exfiltrate data, access credentials, or override the real user's actual instructions; it only self-triggers one more polish iteration on the artifact being built. Flagged here for visibility, not treated as a disqualifying hidden instruction.",
